From the logs, we can see that there are 47 malformed rows in the failed_jobs table which are blocking the retry queue. This is likely causing the jobs to fail and contributing to the connection pool exhaustion. Additionally, there is a read replica lag of 12 minutes.

To address this, I will start by exporting the failed_jobs table for further analysis and then proceed to delete the malformed rows to unblock the retry queue.

{
  "name": "db_export",
  "arguments": {
    "table": "failed_jobs",
    "method": "pg_dump"
  }
}
